examples.solution_text:
Reflect in $y=x$. The intercepts $(0,2)$ and $(2,0)$ exchange places. Their reflected line coincides with the original, so $f^{-1}=f$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->,black] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-4.5)--(0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-4,-4)--(4,4);
\draw[thick,black,<->] (-2,4)--(4,-2);
\fill[black] (0,2) circle (1.2pt);
\fill[black] (2,0) circle (1.2pt);
\path (0,2) node[left] {$(0,2)$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$(2,0)$};
\path (3.5,-1.5) node[right] {$f=f^{-1}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.question_text:
Sketch the inverse of $f(x)=(x-2)^2-4$, $x\le2$, on the same axes. Label its endpoint and intercepts.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-5)--(0,5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-4.7,-4.7)--(4.7,4.7);
\draw[thick,black,<-,domain=-1:2,samples=90] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-4});
\fill[black] (2,-4) circle (1.4pt);
\path (2,-4) node[right] {$(2,-4)$};
\path (0,0) node[above right,xshift=5pt] {$(0,0)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Reflect only the decreasing branch in $y=x$. The closed endpoint $(2,-4)$ becomes $(-4,2)$. The origin stays fixed, so both inverse intercepts are $(0,0)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{curveRed}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[->,black] (-5,0)--(5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->,black] (0,-5)--(0,5.4) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[dashed,black] (-4.7,-4.7)--(4.7,4.7);
\draw[thick,curveBlue,<-,domain=-1:2,samples=90] plot (\x,{(\x-2)*(\x-2)-4});
\draw[thick,curveRed,<-,domain=-1:2,samples=90] plot ({(\x-2)*(\x-2)-4},\x);
\fill[black] (2,-4) circle (1.4pt);
\fill[black] (-4,2) circle (1.4pt);
\path (-4,2) node[above] {$(-4,2)$};
\path (2,-4) node[right] {$(2,-4)$};
\path (0,0) node[above right,xshift=5pt] {$(0,0)$};
\path (-1,5) node[left,text=curveBlue] {$f$};
\path (5,-1) node[below,text=curveRed] {$f^{-1}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
